meantime a clark county school district  teacher retires after decades of  teaching and she was hoping to be paid  for her hundreds of unused sick days but  to her surprise her check was nothing  like she expected now she wants to warn  others she spoke with 8 news now  reporter victoria saha who joins us now  with more victoria  cynthia darcy has been with the district  for over 30 years every year she would  get around 15 sick days but she wouldn't  use many because she knew finding a  substitute would be hard and also in  hopes to cash them out at retirement  which is what the what is written in the  negotiated agreement between the  district and this union after looking  forward to a big check she was  disappointed and took to social media to  warn other teachers  cynthia darcy was dedicated to the clark  county school district for 31 years this  was my first year of teaching check out  that huge 80s hair she took to social  media after receiving her check from the  school district for her unused sick time  in her post she claims she racked up 306  sick days but the negotiated agreement  states only a hundred of those days will  be paid out she shows us her check of  what she was paid for a hundred days her  total was 467 dollars after taxes and it  shows each unused sick day was worth  five dollars and ten cents it's reading  the fine fine print to  learn that they will only pay for a  hundred i did reach out to the school  district to find out exactly how those  daily rates are calculated they referred  me back to the negotiated agreement it  says the district shall allocate the sum  of 196 thousand and 197 dollars and 24  cents and use that amount to come up  with the rate to divide that between the  teachers retiring that year you don't  know how many other teachers are  retiring they don't explain what that  actually means to a single teacher  dorsey claims a substitute shortage  would often times force her to not use  her sick time but what frustrates her is  that throughout most of her career  substitutes would get paid ninety  dollars a day and by her not using a  hundred of those sick days  she saved the school district nine  thousand dollars  and when finding out dr jesus jarrod  will be getting a huge check after being  ousted from his superintendent role  darcy is rethinking her decisions what a  difference i wish i'd used him  earlier this year the school board of  trustees increased the pay of  substitutes from ninety dollars to a  hundred and ten dollars a day darcy  tells me she doesn't regret showing up  for her students even when she was sick  but wish teachers were appreciated more  she hopes her message will allow  teachers to put themselves first
 

